  <content>
  <section><title>Self Check</title>
<para dir="ltr">The graph below represents the temperature, \(t(m)\), in degrees Fahrenheit of water used for a cup of hot tea over time in minutes, \(m\). What does \(t(0)\) represent? </para>
<para dir="ltr"><b id="docs-internal-guid-7964e02d-7fff-f050-5252-00ddca19cf11"><figure><media alt="GRAPH THAT SHOWS TEMPERATURE IN DEGREES FAHRENHEIT AS A FUNCTION OF TIME IN MINUTES WITH A \(y\)-intercepts OF 70. THE GRAPH INCREASES, THEN DECREASES, AND THEN REMAINS CONSTANT."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/53af2afc0c96fc02a8264cbdf88c9777b1db4a7e"/></media></figure></b></para></section>
